WEBVTT

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.950
To infinity and beyond!

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.430
Aw, come on. Princesses
and cartoon characters?

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.910
Lame.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.390
Hey, easy there.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.150
Oh, I mean,
no offense or anything.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.550
Well, time to get to work.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.310
ANNOUNCER:
And for your final question.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.510
"My friends
would describe me as?"

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.750
"Smart, funny,
kind, or brave."

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.830
Um...

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.190
Kind, I guess?

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.830
Based on your answers,
your princess BFF is

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.550
Snow White!

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.030
I do believe our friendship

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.950
will be the fairest
of them all!

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.110
Hey, wanna meet my BFF?
It's Wreck-It Ralph.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.270
Just click here
to see his new video.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:50.510
(BEEPS)

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:51.590
Thank you.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.870
Yeah, um, in Captain America:
The First Avenger...

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:56.630
Red Skull refers to Yggdrasil,

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.950
the World Tree,
Guardian of Wisdom and Fate.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:00.710
Are we to believe, sir,

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.550
that you are a descendant
of that tree?

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:04.910
I am Groot.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.190
Okay, okay.
Thank you very much.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:09.510
Um, what is Drax really like?

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:10.990
-I am Groot.
-Thank you.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:14.190
Yeah. Are you a conifer
or a fruit-bearing tree?

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.270
-I...
-Excuse me.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.550
I'll take this one.
He is Groot,

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.190
I am Vanellope, click here
to meet Wreck-It Ralph.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:22.670
Eh, this is almost too easy.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.950
STORMTROOPER 1: Hey, do you
have a permit for that pop-up?

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.070
Uh...

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.870
That's unauthorized clickbait.
You're coming with us, kid.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.550
-Boop!
-(SCREAMS)

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.190
STORMTROOPER 2:
She's getting away.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.550
(ANNOUNCER CHATTERING)

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:35.630
STORMTROOPER 3: This way.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.070
Ooh!

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.390
Sorry, mister!

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:44.750
Hey, can't you read?
Cast members only!

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:46.710
(VANELLOPE PANTING, EXCLAIMS)

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.150
STORMTROOPER 2: I think she
went down this way. Come on.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.230
STORMTROOPER 3: Roger that.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:50.710
STORMTROOPER 3: Did you see
a kid come through here?

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.510
She came running through here
like a headless hen.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.510
(STRAINING)

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.710
STORMTROOPER 3:
Any sign of her?

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.430
STORMTROOPER 2:
No, maybe she went down

00:01:58.510 --> 00:01:59.630
to the Air Bud pavilion.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.590
STORMTROOPER 3:
Come on. Let's check it out.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.350
(PRINCESSES CHATTERING)

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.470
(PRINCESS HUMMING)

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:08.790
(PRINCESSES GASPING)

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:09.910
Uh, hi!

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.630
(PRINCESSES GRUNTING,
SHOUTING)

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.710
Whoa, whoa.
Ladies, I can explain.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.670
See, I'm a princess, too.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.310
-Wait, what?
-VANELLOPE: Yeah.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.350
Princess Vanellope
Von Schweetz...

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.470
of the, uh, Sugar Rush
Von Schweetzes.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:26.870
I'm sure you've heard of us.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.070
It'd be embarrassing for you
if you haven't.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.150
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.430
Huh. What kind of
a princess are you?

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:33.630
What kind?

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.430
-Do you have magic hair?
-No.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:37.070
-Magic hands?
-No.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.110
-Do animals talk to you?
-No.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.470
-Were you poisoned?
-No!

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:41.630
-BOTH: Cursed?
-No!

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:43.270
-BOTH: Kidnapped or enslaved?
-No!

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.030
Are you guys okay?
Should I call the police?

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.670
Then I have to assume
you made a deal

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.950
with an underwater
sea witch...

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.110
where she took your voice

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.190
in exchange
for a pair of human legs?

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.550
No! Good Lord,
who would do that?

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.430
(SING-SONG) Have you ever had
True Love's Kiss?

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:56.510
Ew! Barf!

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:57.830
Do you have daddy issues?

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.030
I don't even have a mom.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.790
PRINCESSES: Neither do we!

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.150
And now for
the million-dollar question.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.950
Do people assume
all your problems got solved

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.790
because a big strong man
showed up?

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.910
Yes! What is up with that?

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:11.590
ALL: She is a princess!

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.990
(VOCALIZING)

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.470
Who made your gown?

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.230
I've never seen
anything quite like it.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:17.550
Oh, this old thing?

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.630
Oh, I'd so love to
have one of my own.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:20.790
-As would I.
-MOANA: Me too!

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.310
-ELSA: So cool.
-Best outfit ever!

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.670
Ooh! I want one, too,
you guys!

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.470
I'll get my mice on this.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:28.230
(SIGHS)

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.390
So this is love.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:34.830
All hail Princess Vanellope,
the queen of comfy!

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:36.710
-(PRINCESSES CHEERING)
-RAPUNZEL: Yay, Vanellope!

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.510
Of all the thingamabobs
in this entire world...

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:41.910
I never thought
I'd get to wear a real...

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.390
what's it called again?

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.310
Oh, yeah. Shirt.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:49.590
(SINGING) I once had a dream
that I might wear a shirt...

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.990
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Wait! What's going on?

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:53.950
Uh, she's singing.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:57.110
Yeah, but there was like music
and a spotlight.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.950
Wait, you all saw it too,
right?

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.230
That's what happens

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:02.230
when a princess
sings about her dreams.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:05.750
Oh, that's never happened
to me. I mean, not even once.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.470
Why don't you give it a try?

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:10.630
What is it you really want?
Sing about that.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.070
Okay. Uh, sure.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.990
Huh. I could do that.
Um, let's see.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:15.590
(CLEARS THROAT)

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:20.430
(SINGING) Oh, steering wheel
Oh, steering wheel

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:23.990
Oh, yes
I want a steering wheel

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.550
(SCATTING)

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.510
Well, there is a lot
to unpack here.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:30.630
AURORA: Mmm-hmm.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.190
So, this steering wheel
you sing of,

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:34.550
that's a metaphor?

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.910
Oh, no, no, no, it's not
a metaphor. I just...

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.310
I literally want
a steering wheel.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.750
I think the issue is
I was a little pitchy.

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.150
Maybe a little.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:46.390
But sometimes
your song can't start...

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.870
until you go someplace
to reflect.

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.190
What works for some of us...

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:54.910
is finding a form of water
and staring at it.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:56.670
What?

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.150
Oh, yes, I like to stare
at a wishing well!

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.550
I stare at the ocean.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:01.710
Horse trough.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:02.950
Soap bubbles!

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.710
Wait, you're saying if I just
stare at some water...

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:08.030
Uh, important water.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.630
Right. Of course.
"Important water."

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.990
I stare at
the important water...

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:16.310
and somehow magically I'll
start singing about my dream?

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:17.590
RAPUNZEL: For sure.
TIANA: Mmm-hmm.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.270
Uh, yeah, I don't think so,
ladies, but thanks.

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.350
(KNOCKS ON DOOR)

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.430
C-3PO: Five minutes,
Princesses.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.310
Another "Which Disney Princess
Are You?" quizlet

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:27.790
starts in five minutes.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.310
-(PRINCESSES GROAN)
-JASMINE: Okay, thank you.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:33.270
Well, I guess it's back
to the gowns, girls.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.310
It was lovely to meet you,
Vanellope.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:37.510
And best of luck
finding your song.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:40.550
(SPEAKING SCOTTISH ENGLISH)

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.030
Uh-huh.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.310
(WHISPERING)
What did she just say?

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:49.150
-We don't know.
-We can't understand her.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:50.950
She's from the other studio.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.110
Ah.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.630
RALPH: Hi, everybody.
Wreck-It Ralph here... RALPH: Hi, everybody.
Wreck-It Ralph here...

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.310
with a little box
I'm gonna open.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:58.990
Let's see what we got here.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:02.310
A "Pancake Milkshake Fun Set."
Huh.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:03.710
Got a little heft to it.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.430
Something wobbling around
in there.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.070
Wonder if we got
the kitty or the bunny.

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:08.310
Let's open it up.

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:09.830
-(BUZZING)
-(RALPH SCREAMING)

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:12.110
(ANNOUNCER READING)

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:13.830
Man, who would've
guessed a bee pun

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:15.990
would be the thing
to put us over the top?

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:17.990
Huh.
That's the Internet for you.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:21.030
All right, it is uploading.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.350
Hey, mister!

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:23.430
(GASPS) Oh. Hi, eboy.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:24.990
Just here to let you know

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.510
your bid does expire
in 30 minutes.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:29.670
(SIGHS) Thanks, little eboy.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:30.870
You got it, chairman.

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:32.510
You hear that, Yesss?

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:33.910
We don't have
a lot of time left.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:35.470
-Okay. We just gotta...
-(COMPUTER BUZZES)

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:37.590
No, no, no.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.310
No! Not you!

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.070
What? Why are you
angry at the lollipop?

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:42.150
What does that mean?

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.550
(GROANS)
The file's not loading.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.510
If this doesn't load,
we're not gonna make it.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.950
-Hmm.
-You don't have enough hearts.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:49.750
Ralph, where are you going?

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:51.550
I'm going down to the floor
to get some hearts.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:53.270
Ah! Genius! Good thinking.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.670
Now, someone get me
tech support in here, stat!

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.830
-(PANTING)
-(RALPH SHOUTING ON VIDEO)

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:00.950
RALPH: Only one person.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.550
Hey, guys, come and
check out my video,

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:03.630
you're gonna love it.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:06.430
Right, right over here.
Yep, here we go.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:08.550
What are you...
You guys!

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.190
Aw. A cat?

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:14.430
You're gonna like this better
than some dusty old cat.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.230
Aw.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:17.350
What?

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.070
Give me that hose, partner.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:22.550
You know you love me, give me
those hearts. There we go.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:25.310
Hey, folks, where are you
going? Give my video a heart.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.310
That's it.
Let's see who's in here.

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:29.830
Hello?

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:32.550
Anybody in here?

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:37.110
What the heck is this place?

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:40.590
Some kind of libary?

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.950
"Wreck-It Ralph is back."

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.470
Hey, they're talking about me.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:49.550
Gee whiz,
the Internet is so positive.

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:52.350
"Fix-It Felix, Jr.
was my favorite game."

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.070
Hmm. Mine, too.

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:56.430
"Ralph's videos stink."

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:58.110
What?

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:00.070
"So stupid."

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:02.550
"Ralph is the worst."

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:05.430
"I hate him."

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:08.870
"He's so fat and ugly."

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:15.630
"Just a worthless bum,
alone on a pile of bricks."

